# ============================================
# Inbox Copilot Frontend Environment Configuration
# ============================================
#
# This file serves as a template for environment-specific configuration.
# Copy this file to `.env` and update the values for your environment.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit the actual `.env` file to version control!
# The `.env` file should be added to .gitignore.
#
# ============================================

# --------------------------------------------
# API Configuration
# --------------------------------------------

# REACT_APP_API_URL
# 
# The base URL for the backend API server.
# This URL is used by the frontend to make all API requests.
#
# Local Development:
#   Use http://localhost:8000 when running the backend locally
#   Example: REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
#
# Production:
#   Use your deployed backend URL (e.g., Heroku, AWS, Azure, etc.)
#   Example: REACT_APP_API_URL=https://api.inboxcopilot.com
#   Example: REACT_APP_API_URL=https://your-app.herokuapp.com
#
# Staging/Testing:
#   Use your staging environment URL
#   Example: REACT_APP_API_URL=https://staging-api.inboxcopilot.com
#
# Default: http://localhost:8000 (if not set)
#
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --------------------------------------------
# Setup Instructions
# --------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Copy this file:
#    cp .env.example .env
#
# 2. Update REACT_APP_API_URL in .env to match your backend URL
#
# 3. Restart the development server for changes to take effect:
#    npm start
#
# 4. Verify the configuration:
#    - Open browser console
#    - Check that API requests are going to the correct URL
#    - Look for CORS errors if using a different domain
#
# --------------------------------------------
# Environment-Specific Examples
# --------------------------------------------
#
# Local Development (default):
# REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
#
# Local Development (custom port):
# REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
#
# Docker Compose:
# REACT_APP_API_URL=http://backend:8000
#
# Production (Heroku):
# REACT_APP_API_URL=https://inbox-copilot-api.herokuapp.com
#
# Production (AWS):
# REACT_APP_API_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# Production (Custom Domain):
# REACT_APP_API_URL=https://api.inboxcopilot.com
#
# --------------------------------------------
# Troubleshooting
# --------------------------------------------
#
# Issue: API requests failing with CORS errors
# Solution: Ensure the backend CORS configuration allows requests from your frontend origin
#
# Issue: Environment variable not updating
# Solution: Restart the React development server (npm start)
#
# Issue: 404 errors on API endpoints
# Solution: Verify the backend is running and accessible at the configured URL
#
# Issue: Connection refused errors
# Solution: Check that the backend server is running and the port is correct
#
# --------------------------------------------
# Additional Notes
# --------------------------------------------
#
# - All React environment variables must start with REACT_APP_
# - Environment variables are embedded at build time, not runtime
# - For production builds, set the correct REACT_APP_API_URL before running `npm run build`
# - The config.js file provides a fallback to http://localhost:8000 if this variable is not set
#
